{
  "updated": "2026-10-21",
  "notes": [
    "One entry per video model, in the order the model picker lists them; the first model serving a mode is that mode's default.",
    "id: stored in jobs, templates and settings; never change an existing one. title, family and detail are the English fallbacks of the keys <id>.title, <id>.family and <id>.detail in Models.xcstrings.",
    "resolutions: the ones the model renders at, when not all of 480p, 720p and 1080p (also 768p and 2K, which only MiniMax has); the picker offers these and a job asking for another gets the nearest. pricing.json needs each.",
    "aspectRatios: the frames a REST body may name, for a schema whose aspect_ratio has no 'follow the source' value; the body names the one nearest the source's frame. Left out, so is the field.",
    "limits: [min, max] over the mode's own (Mode.limits); the server's models_explore answer still overrides them bound by bound.",
    "controls: draft, clipWithoutSource (length and frame without a source video), generatedAudio, bitrate, frames, quality (Standard/Pro instead of a resolution), characterOrientation, videoBackground, cinemaControls (Cinema Studio's camera, lens, genre, era and the rest; their titles are cinemaStudio4.<field> and cinemaStudio4.<field>.<value> in Models.xcstrings).",
    "request.shape: the code that encodes the body (genjutsu, seedance, klingMotionControl, klingVideoReference, klingVideoEdit, wanReference, cinemaStudio). request.endpoints: the REST endpoint by the first key that applies: the mode, frames, standard/pro, reference (with media) or text, then default. Every endpoint needs rates in pricing.json. Empty for a model the public REST docs don't list: it runs on the account only, and an API key isn't offered it.",
    "request.account: the account's generate_video model ID by mode, once its models_explore get schema confirms every field the shape sends (the snapshot tests check it); a model without one runs with an API key only.",
    "requiresPrompt: a job needs a prompt even with a source.",
    "credits: the account's fallback estimate, base + perSecond[resolution] x billed seconds, rounded up; modes overrides it for a mode priced apart. The price Create shows is Higgsfield's get_cost quote: before upload for a model sent a length, after upload for one billed by its source (Genjutsu, Edit). The estimate stands in only until then, or when the quote fails. Rates from free get_cost quotes of 2026-10-15 (issue #113). Left out (or a resolution missing), a job the server can't quote shows 'Price unknown'."
  ],
